    "updated_at": "2024-04-09T10:55:55Z",
    "body": "It's hard to think of a case that would reliably fail as typically a dedicated worker is in the same agent cluster as its owner. And in the one case where that might not be the case (`data:` URLs and sandboxing) the dedicated worker is less privileged so you could not use `SharedArrayBuffer` as test. And beyond `SharedArrayBuffer` I'm not sure there's a good `messageerror` example, except for the theoretical one around OOO.\r\n\r\n@foolip what you're looking for is described here: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dedicated-workers-and-the-worker-interface\r\n\r\n> All messages received by that port must immediately be retargeted at the [Worker](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#worker) object.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
