    "created_at": "2026-05-04T13:35:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-05-04T13:35:58Z",
    "body": "Current status: `onmessageerror` should be there as that just makes sense and there are theoretical cases where `messageerror` can fire. We can keep this open for someone to come up with a good test. Eventually there will be some kind of object that can serialize in a dedicated worker but cannot deserialize in a window or shared worker environment.",
